+# V3 punctual recovery/evidence correction, source-only, NOT activated
+
+Supersedes V2 recovery wording only. No new OCI research, extraction, network/probe/unit/npm/compiler/test effects. Candidate/FS11/offline/fulltypes/filters/gate/overlay oracles unchanged. This delta edits producer/network plus this review and finite delta metadata.
+
+HOLD correction: reconcile_owned() no longer invokes network.cleanup AT ALL. Persisted JSON cannot recreate held cgroup/pidfd custody and cannot prove a destroyed identity was the originally acquired one. Therefore recovery retains network/namespace/nft/veth/unitfile/evidence for disposableVMteardown, even if systemctlstop acknowledged and managerPIDs are0. It reports noLiveWritersProved=false, blocker HELD_CGROUP_CUSTODY_NOT_RECOVERABLE_FROM_JSON and UNKNOWN. It does NOT fabricate current no-live-writers evidence from a historical record, mutate network after a failed stop, or convert conservative retention into PASS.
+
+A recovery stop request itself requires exact sourcehash/rootownership/mode of ownunitfile, durable acquiredadmission binding unit/InvocationID/controlgroup and current manager SAMEInvocation/no restarts. Missing admission or replaced invocation means NO stop either. Stopintent durable before request, failure remains recorded. A valid stop is progress only, never permission to remove red/evidence. This deliberately chooses the requested conservative retain-for-teardown path rather than adding a new observer to recover losthandles.
+
+Normal preparation immediately persists anchor.record and acquiredunitidentity BEFORE later admissionreads/permissions, closing the interval where recovery might otherwise lack identity. Existing normal path STILL proves whole acquiredcgroupterminal A/B BEFORE networkcleanup and keeps heldhandles through independentOOM; that reviewed order is unchanged.
+
+Evidence correction: earlyexport is now explicitly network-ledger-before-cleanup.json. After normalcleanup attempts, copy actual FINAL originalledger into selected/network-ledger.json and record exact bytecount/SHA/copyAfterCleanupAttempt. REMOVAL_VERIFIED or UNKNOWN/failures are the final version actually delivered, not earlierACK. If finalcopy fails, evidenceUnknown→UNKNOWN. No finalcopy when terminal was not proven and selection stayed unavailable; resources/evidence stay inVM.
+
+Guarantee labels: each deletion using known inode/ifindex/nfttablehandle says ACQUIRED_*_MATCH. If a prior command result was uncertain BEFORE identitycapture, cleanup explicitly says PREFLIGHT_ABSENT_EXACT_RESERVED_NAME_NO_PRIOR_KERNEL_IDENTITY. It never promotes exact reservedname into acquiredkernelidentity. Scope remains one durable randomrunreservation, no prefixsweep.
+
+No launcher/wiringoffline/probes/services authorized or run. All v2 realenvironmentpreconditions remain, no newpermissions. These functions are proposals for review only. Source syntax parsed and unchanged files byte-compared; no custommodule imports.
+
+---
+
